IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2019: redemption of program benefits.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Seam taken as an input, named for the answering section: s 2012(o)(4) (the keel holds paragraph (4) as a field, not a function).
-- Section 2019 is one paragraph of three sentences; each function cites the sentence (or the limb of the first sentence) it implements.

-- src:1422 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for the redemption of benefits accepted by retail food stores through approved wholesale food concerns or through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, or which are insured under the Federal Credit Union Act [12 U.S.C. 1751 et seq.] and have retail food stores or wholesale food concerns in their field of membership, with the cooperation of the Treasury Department,
@ref s 2019, first sentence, the channels (src:1422)
GIVEN `the channel is an approved wholesale food concern` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the channel is a financial institution which is insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the channel is a financial institution which is insured under the Federal Credit Union Act and has retail food stores or wholesale food concerns in its field of membership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2019 the channel is one through which benefits accepted by retail food stores are redeemed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the channel is an approved wholesale food concern` OR `the channel is a financial institution which is insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation` OR `the channel is a financial institution which is insured under the Federal Credit Union Act and has retail food stores or wholesale food concerns in its field of membership`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Regulations ... shall provide for the redemption of benefits accepted by retail food stores through approved wholesale food concerns or through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names three channels and does not close the list with "only"

-- src:1422 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for the redemption of benefits accepted by retail food stores through approved wholesale food concerns or through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, or which are insured under the Federal Credit Union Act [12 U.S.C. 1751 et seq.] and have retail food stores or wholesale food concerns in their field of membership, with the cooperation of the Treasury Department, except that retail food stores defined in section 2012(o)(4) of this title shall be authorized to redeem their members’ food benefits prior to receipt by the members of the food so purchased, retail food stores authorized to accept and redeem benefits through on-line transactions shall be authorized to accept benefits prior to the delivery of food if the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary, and publicly operated community mental health centers or private nonprofit organizations or institutions which serve meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs, public and private nonprofit shelters that prepare and serve meals for battered women and children, and public or private nonprofit group living arrangements that serve meals to disabled or blind residents, shall not be authorized to redeem benefits through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or the Federal Credit Union Act. Notwithstanding the preceding sentence, a center, organization, institution, shelter, group living arrangement, or establishment described in that sentence may be authorized to redeem benefits through a financial institution described in that sentence if the center, organization, institution, shelter, group living arrangement, or establishment is equipped with 1 or more point-of-sale devices and is operating in an area in which an electronic benefit transfer system described in section 2016(h) of this title has been implemented. No financial institution may impose on or collect from a retail food store a fee or other charge for the redemption of benefits that are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements, other than any requirements relating to cancellation of benefits, for the presentation of benefits by financial institutions to the Federal Reserve banks.
@ref s 2019, first sentence, the first exception (src:1422)
GIVEN `s 2012(o)(4) the seller is a private nonprofit cooperative food purchasing venture or an agricultural producer marketing directly to consumers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2019 the retail food store is authorized to redeem the members' food benefits before the members receive the food` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(o)(4) the seller is a private nonprofit cooperative food purchasing venture or an agricultural producer marketing directly to consumers`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "retail food stores defined in section 2012(o)(4) of this title shall be authorized to redeem their members' food benefits prior to receipt by the members of the food so purchased"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for "retail food stores defined in section 2012(o)(4)"

-- src:1422 | Regulations issued pursuant to this chapter shall provide for the redemption of benefits accepted by retail food stores through approved wholesale food concerns or through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, or which are insured under the Federal Credit Union Act [12 U.S.C. 1751 et seq.] and have retail food stores or wholesale food concerns in their field of membership, with the cooperation of the Treasury Department, except that retail food stores defined in section 2012(o)(4) of this title shall be authorized to redeem their members’ food benefits prior to receipt by the members of the food so purchased, retail food stores authorized to accept and redeem benefits through on-line transactions shall be authorized to accept benefits prior to the delivery of food if the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary, and publicly operated community mental health centers or private nonprofit organizations or institutions which serve meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs, public and private nonprofit shelters that prepare and serve meals for battered women and children, and public or private nonprofit group living arrangements that serve meals to disabled or blind residents, shall not be authorized to redeem benefits through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or the Federal Credit Union Act. Notwithstanding the preceding sentence, a center, organization, institution, shelter, group living arrangement, or establishment described in that sentence may be authorized to redeem benefits through a financial institution described in that sentence if the center, organization, institution, shelter, group living arrangement, or establishment is equipped with 1 or more point-of-sale devices and is operating in an area in which an electronic benefit transfer system described in section 2016(h) of this title has been implemented. No financial institution may impose on or collect from a retail food store a fee or other charge for the redemption of benefits that are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements, other than any requirements relating to cancellation of benefits, for the presentation of benefits by financial institutions to the Federal Reserve banks.
@ref s 2019, first sentence, the second exception (src:1422)
GIVEN `the retail food store is authorized to accept and redeem benefits through on-line transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2019 the retail food store is authorized to accept benefits before the delivery of the food` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the retail food store is authorized to accept and redeem benefits through on-line transactions`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for "retail food stores authorized to accept and redeem benefits through on-line transactions"
        IF `the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be authorized to accept benefits prior to the delivery of food if the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the delivery occurs within a reasonable time of the purchase, as determined by the Secretary" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:1422 | and publicly operated community mental health centers or private nonprofit organizations or institutions which serve meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs, public and private nonprofit shelters that prepare and serve meals for battered women and children, and public or private nonprofit group living arrangements that serve meals to disabled or blind residents, shall not be authorized to redeem benefits through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or the Federal Credit Union Act.
@ref s 2019, first and second sentences, the centres, organizations, shelters and arrangements (src:1422)
GIVEN `the body is a publicly operated community mental health center` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a private nonprofit organization or institution which serves meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a public or private nonprofit shelter that prepares and serves meals for battered women and children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a public or private nonprofit group living arrangement that serves meals to disabled or blind residents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is equipped with 1 or more point-of-sale devices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is operating in an area in which an electronic benefit transfer system described in section 2016(h) has been implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2019 the body may be authorized to redeem benefits through a financial institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the body is a publicly operated community mental health center` OR `the body is a private nonprofit organization or institution which serves meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs` OR `the body is a public or private nonprofit shelter that prepares and serves meals for battered women and children` OR `the body is a public or private nonprofit group living arrangement that serves meals to disabled or blind residents`)
           AND `the body is equipped with 1 or more point-of-sale devices` AND `the body is operating in an area in which an electronic benefit transfer system described in section 2016(h) has been implemented`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a center, organization, institution, shelter, group living arrangement, or establishment described in that sentence may be authorized to redeem benefits through a financial institution described in that sentence if the center ... is equipped with 1 or more point-of-sale devices and is operating in an area in which an electronic benefit transfer system described in section 2016(h) of this title has been implemented"
        IF `the body is a publicly operated community mental health center` OR `the body is a private nonprofit organization or institution which serves meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics in drug addiction or alcoholic treatment and rehabilitation programs` OR `the body is a public or private nonprofit shelter that prepares and serves meals for battered women and children` OR `the body is a public or private nonprofit group living arrangement that serves meals to disabled or blind residents`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "publicly operated community mental health centers or private nonprofit organizations or institutions which serve meals to narcotics addicts or alcoholics ... shall not be authorized to redeem benefits through financial institutions which are insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation or the Federal Credit Union Act"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar names four kinds of body and does not say what applies to others

-- src:1422 | No financial institution may impose on or collect from a retail food store a fee or other charge for the redemption of benefits that are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements, other than any requirements relating to cancellation of benefits, for the presentation of benefits by financial institutions to the Federal Reserve banks.
@ref s 2019, third sentence (src:1422)
GIVEN `the benefits are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements, other than any requirements relating to cancellation of benefits, for the presentation of benefits by financial institutions to the Federal Reserve banks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2019 the financial institution may impose on or collect from the retail food store a fee or other charge for the redemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefits are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements, other than any requirements relating to cancellation of benefits, for the presentation of benefits by financial institutions to the Federal Reserve banks`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No financial institution may impose on or collect from a retail food store a fee or other charge for the redemption of benefits that are submitted to the financial institution in a manner consistent with the requirements"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a fee "for the redemption of benefits that are submitted ... in a manner consistent with the requirements"
